            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Move to Rome</strong><br>\nPope Julius II invited Raphael to Rome in 1508 to work on the Vatican palaces. This marked the beginning of Raphael's career as a sought-after artist in Rome. He worked on several commissions there, painting frescoes that showcased his mastery of large-scale compositions and his ability to convey complex narratives.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Stanza Della Segnatura</strong><br>\nOne of Raphael's most famous works is the frescoes in the Stanza della Segnatura, which include \"The School of Athens.\" This particular fresco illustrates an idealized gathering of philosophers and scientists and serves as a symbol of the Renaissance spirit, celebrating the rebirth of classical knowledge and wisdom.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Architectural Work</strong><br>\nBesides painting, Raphael was also involved in architecture. After the death of Donato Bramante, Raphael was appointed as the chief architect of Saint Peter's Basilica in Rome. His architectural works demonstrated his versatility and contributed to the development of High Renaissance style in architecture.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
